const title = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 3 Level 7 Walkthrough: Master Bathroom";
const description = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 3 Level 7 walkthrough for Master Bathroom: the six-dial cistern panel that takes 279151 from the three numbered tiles 27, 91 and 51, and the four-digit door keypad that takes 6389 off the shower wall tiles.";

const faq = [
  {
    q: "What is the code in Rooms & Exits Chapter 3 Level 7 Master Bathroom?",
    a: "There are two keypads and two codes. The <b>six-dial panel on the toilet cistern</b> takes <b>279151</b>, built from the three numbered tiles that sit on the cistern lid: <b>27</b>, <b>91</b> and <b>51</b>. The <b>four-digit keypad on the door</b>, the black panel with a red display, takes <b>6389</b>, the four digits printed on the shower wall tiles. Both were read at least twice from separate frames, and the cistern code was confirmed on the frame where the panel closed and the lid opened.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where does 279151 come from?",
    a: "From the three tiles on top of the toilet cistern. Reading the slots left to right gives <b>27</b> on the parallelogram tile, <b>91</b> on the oval tile and <b>51</b> on the rhombus tile — six digits in a row, <b>2 7 9 1 5 1</b>. The six buttons on the front of the cistern are turned to that value and the lid releases.",
  },
  {
    q: "Why does the middle tile look like 16 instead of 91?",
    a: "Because it rotates. The oval tile sits in a slot with a curved arrow above it, and in the recording it is first placed reading <b>16</b>. Turn it 180 degrees and the same tile reads <b>91</b>. The cistern only opens with the rotated value, which is why 279151 works and 271651 does not.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where is the 6389 clue?",
    a: "On the shower wall. Stand at the shower, look at the beige rectangular tiles to the right of the handheld sprayer, and four light-coloured digits are set into the tiling: <b>6 3 8 9</b>. It is easy to walk past because the shower is the last place you would look for a number, and the digits are the same tone as the grout.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where do I enter 6389?",
    a: "On the door. The wooden door has a black keypad with a red four-digit display above a yellow 1-9 grid, a yellow X and a yellow enter arrow. Type <b>6389</b> and confirm; in the recording the display holds <b>6389</b> in black on red and the door swings ajar at 3:12, showing the orange door icon that ends the room.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the 'Arrange the light on the drawer like that on the mirror' puzzle?",
    a: "It is the vanity puzzle at <b>0:24</b>. The instruction banner reads exactly that, and the target pattern is reflected in the two mirrors above the sinks while the drawers below carry the lights you move. The recording solves it but never holds a clean shot of the solved drawer, so this page does not print a pattern for it — copying a guessed arrangement would only get you a wrong answer.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is 'Order of the towels'?",
    a: "A second instruction banner, at <b>1:04</b>, over the towel rack in the toilet alcove. The rack holds several folded grey towels and the game wants them in a set order. As with the drawer lights, we could not read the required order off the footage, so no sequence is printed here.",
  },
  {
    q: "What does the floor drain do?",
    a: "The square metal drain on the tiled floor between the bathtub and the side table is a hotspot at <b>0:42</b>. In the recording the player zooms on it right after opening the vanity cabinets, which suggests it is where a tool gets used, but the action itself happens off-camera between cuts. Treat the drain as a place to check with the screwdriver in your bag rather than as a code.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the cube puzzle?",
    a: "A floating cube of yellow and dark-red blocks appears at <b>2:16</b>, and the banner at <b>2:25</b> reads <b>Touch order for the cube</b>. Later, at <b>2:34</b>, the same pattern is shown flattened as a 3x3 grid of yellow, green and maroon triangles. The sequence itself is a touch order, not a number, and we could not read the order reliably from one frame per second — it is listed as unverified on this page.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is Master Bathroom the seventh room of Chapter 3?",
    a: "Yes. Chapter 3 is <i>Murder Dressed in White</i>, and Master Bathroom is room <b>7 of 15</b>, after Workshop (5) and Guest Bedroom (6), before Kids Playroom (8). The room is the largest in the chapter so far: a double vanity wall, a freestanding tub, a walk-in glass shower and a separate toilet alcove behind a partition.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the reward for finishing Master Bathroom?",
    a: "We cannot tell you. The recording runs 3:15 and the last clear gameplay frame is the door swinging ajar at <b>3:12</b> with the exit icon; after that the picture fades out at 3:15 without a LEVEL COMPLETED card, a coin figure or a results panel. Since we have not seen the reward, this page does not print one.",
  },
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.a.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, "") },
  })),
};
