    <h2>What this page could not verify<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="warn">
      Four things, stated plainly so you know which parts of this page are reads and which are reconstruction.
      <br><br>
      <b>1. The drawer-light pattern.</b> We have the instruction word for word — "Arrange the light on the drawer like that on the mirror" — and we can see the player complete it, but no frame in the recording holds a clean view of the solved drawer or the mirror pattern it has to match. Any arrangement printed here would be invented, so none is.
      <br><br>
      <b>2. The towel order.</b> Same problem. The banner "Order of the towels" is legible at 1:04; the sequence the rack wants is not, because the towels are handled between cuts. If you find the answer in your own run, it is worth writing down — the recording does not give it to us.
      <br><br>
      <b>3. The cube's touch order.</b> The banner at 2:25 is clear and the flattened 3x3 grid is visible around 2:34, but the order of taps happens faster than one frame per second can carry. We can tell you it is a sequence puzzle and that a wrong touch resets it; we cannot tell you the sequence.
      <br><br>
      <b>4. The reward and the results panel.</b> The video ends at 3:15, three seconds after the door opens, on a fade. No LEVEL COMPLETED card, no coin figure, no results screen. We do not print a reward for Master Bathroom because we have not seen one — the number would be a guess, and this page does not guess numbers.
